1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:14,924
All 5 cards from lessons 11–15 – full dialogues with the examiner. Plus 12 questions that fit almost any card and 5 mistakes that cost points. Get ready and ask out loud!

2
00:00:15,833 --> 00:00:30,323
How does task 2 work? You get two cards with a situation. On each card you ask four questions: three from the hints and one of your own. The examiner answers. You can get twelve points in total.

3
00:00:31,233 --> 00:00:44,189
The card has only short hints. You must turn them into a full polite question. Now we go through all five cards. First ask yourself, then you hear a model question and the examiner’s answer.

4
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:48,188
Card 11: You are at a car service.

5
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:52,109
You are at a car repair shop. You need your car repaired.

6
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:55,795
Good afternoon. How can I help you?

7
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,333
Hello, when will the car be ready?

8
00:01:04,533 --> 00:01:06,367
The car will be ready on Friday.

9
00:01:12,567 --> 00:01:14,200
How much will the repair cost?

10
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:16,688
The repair will cost about 6,000 crowns.

11
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:24,689
Can you lend me a replacement car?

12
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:27,056
Yes, we can lend you a replacement car.

13
00:01:33,267 --> 00:01:34,887
Can I pay by card?

14
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:37,319
Yes, you can pay by card or in cash.

15
00:01:37,533 --> 00:01:40,533
Thank you for the information. Goodbye.

16
00:01:40,733 --> 00:01:41,886
Goodbye.

17
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:48,497
Is this helping? Subscribe – there is a new video every day. And now the next card.

18
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:51,920
Card 12: You are in a supermarket.

19
00:01:52,233 --> 00:01:55,332
You are in a supermarket looking for goods.

20
00:01:56,533 --> 00:01:58,133
Hello, can I help you?

21
00:02:04,333 --> 00:02:06,455
Hello, where can I find milk?

22
00:02:06,667 --> 00:02:09,300
Milk is in the fridge at the back.

23
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:16,933
Do you have fresh bread?

24
00:02:17,133 --> 00:02:19,400
Yes, we bake bread every morning.

25
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:27,067
Is there a discount today?

26
00:02:27,267 --> 00:02:29,333
Yes, fruit is on sale today.

27
00:02:35,533 --> 00:02:37,333
What time do you close?

28
00:02:37,533 --> 00:02:39,692
We're open until 10 pm.

29
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:42,900
Thank you for the information. Goodbye.

30
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:44,100
You're welcome.

31
00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:47,298
Card 13: You are at a fitness centre.

32
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:50,723
You are at a fitness centre and want to start working out.

33
00:02:51,933 --> 00:02:54,428
Good afternoon. How can I help you?

34
00:03:00,633 --> 00:03:02,763
Hello, when are you open?

35
00:03:02,967 --> 00:03:06,324
We're open from 6 am to 10 pm.

36
00:03:12,533 --> 00:03:14,400
How much is a monthly pass?

37
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:16,432
A month costs 990 crowns.

38
00:03:22,633 --> 00:03:23,967
Do you have a trainer?

39
00:03:24,167 --> 00:03:26,400
Yes, a trainer is here every day.

40
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:33,667
Is there a shower here?

41
00:03:33,867 --> 00:03:35,464
Yes, the showers are in the changing room.

42
00:03:35,667 --> 00:03:38,667
Thank you for the information. Goodbye.

43
00:03:38,867 --> 00:03:40,067
We look forward to seeing you.

44
00:03:40,267 --> 00:03:43,272
Card 14: You are at an estate agency.

45
00:03:43,567 --> 00:03:47,199
You are at an estate agency. You are looking for a flat to rent.

46
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:50,895
Good afternoon. How can I help you?

47
00:03:57,100 --> 00:03:59,800
Hello, do you have a 2+1 flat available?

48
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:02,000
Yes, we have a 2+1 flat available.

49
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:09,664
How much is the rent?

50
00:04:09,867 --> 00:04:11,824
The rent is 14,000 crowns.

51
00:04:18,033 --> 00:04:19,767
When can I come for a viewing?

52
00:04:19,967 --> 00:04:21,557
A viewing is possible tomorrow.

53
00:04:27,767 --> 00:04:28,833
Can I have a dog?

54
00:04:29,033 --> 00:04:30,967
The owner will allow a small dog.

55
00:04:31,167 --> 00:04:34,167
Thank you for the information. Goodbye.

56
00:04:34,367 --> 00:04:35,519
Goodbye.

57
00:04:35,733 --> 00:04:38,446
Card 15: You are at a government office.

58
00:04:38,733 --> 00:04:42,470
You are at the office. You want to change the address in your documents.

59
00:04:43,667 --> 00:04:46,161
Good afternoon. How can I help you?

60
00:04:52,367 --> 00:04:56,533
Hello, I need to change my address. Where do I get the form?

61
00:04:56,733 --> 00:04:58,500
You can get the form here from me.

62
00:05:04,700 --> 00:05:06,033
How much is the fee?

63
00:05:06,233 --> 00:05:07,633
The fee is 100 crowns.

64
00:05:13,833 --> 00:05:15,183
How long does it take?

65
00:05:15,400 --> 00:05:16,789
It takes about 30 days.

66
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,600
Do I need a tenancy agreement?

67
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:28,333
Yes, bring the tenancy agreement or a confirmation from the owner.

68
00:05:28,533 --> 00:05:31,533
Thank you for the information. Goodbye.

69
00:05:31,733 --> 00:05:32,886
Goodbye.

70
00:05:33,100 --> 00:05:39,083
Now twelve questions that fit almost every card. Listen and repeat out loud.

71
00:05:39,767 --> 00:05:40,951
How much does it cost?

72
00:05:44,167 --> 00:05:45,467
When does the course start?

73
00:05:48,667 --> 00:05:50,467
What time are you open?

74
00:05:53,667 --> 00:05:55,017
How long does it take?

75
00:05:58,233 --> 00:05:59,867
Where is the nearest stop?

76
00:06:03,067 --> 00:06:05,126
Do you have this jacket in a bigger size?

77
00:06:08,333 --> 00:06:09,954
Can I pay by card?

78
00:06:13,167 --> 00:06:14,667
Do I have to change trains?

79
00:06:17,867 --> 00:06:19,500
What do I have to bring with me?

80
00:06:22,700 --> 00:06:24,167
Is it possible to return it?

81
00:06:27,367 --> 00:06:29,033
How do I get to the station?

82
00:06:32,233 --> 00:06:34,800
Could you tell me where the ticket office is?

83
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:41,058
Five typical mistakes that cost people points.

84
00:06:44,267 --> 00:06:50,551
Correct: Kolik to stojí? Don’t just read the word from the card. Ask a full question.

85
00:06:54,267 --> 00:07:01,661
Correct: Můžu platit kartou? You must ask, not state. A question ends with a question mark.

86
00:07:05,367 --> 00:07:12,190
Correct: Máte volný termín? With the examiner you speak formally: máte, můžete.

87
00:07:15,900 --> 00:07:24,052
Correct: Kdy jede vlak do Brna? Put the question word first: kdy, kde, kolik.

88
00:07:27,767 --> 00:07:36,823
Correct: Je tam parkoviště? Prepare the fourth question in advance. Good ones: Je tam parkoviště? Můžu přijít i v sobotu?

89
00:07:38,033 --> 00:07:56,082
Summary. First: turn the hint into a full question. Second: speak formally — máte, můžete. Third: put the question word first. And fourth: have your own question ready.

90
00:07:57,267 --> 00:08:07,424
